    "created_at": "2024-03-25T01:39:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-25T01:39:46Z",
    "body": "Having been involved with server push and a number of other features that were good on paper, I'm extremely cautious about claims of advantage for anything in this approximate area.  Well documented experiments with robust experimental design is what I'm looking for.  Including evidence that the operational costs are manageable and that the performance degradation resulting from operational neglect is tolerable.  That sort of thing.\r\n\r\nAll of that being said, why are you not defining a link relation in the IETF documents?  The HTML-specific processing here seems pretty limited, but the general applicability of the mechanism potentially extends beyond the web.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
